>> title: Beurre Blanc
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: butter, wine, french, fish, stovetop
>> counters: Pizzeria
>> aka: white butter sauce, butter sauce
>> servings: 4
>> time: 25 min
>> slack: unforgiving — let the reduction boil and the emulsion splits into oil and sour wine, and it cannot be held over heat or reheated

>> step: reduce to 2 Tbs
Reduce @dry white wine{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @white wine vinegar{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @shallot{2%Tbs}(minced), and @white peppercorns{1/2%tsp}(cracked) to about 2 Tbs.

>> step: simmer
Simmer @heavy cream{2%Tbs}(30 mL) into @&(~1)reduction{}.

>> step: whisk in cold butter
Whisk @cold unsalted butter{1%cup}(225 g; cut in cubes) into @&(~1)base{} a few cubes at a time, off and on low heat, never letting it boil.

>> step: season and strain
Season @&(~1)sauce{} with @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} and @fresh lemon juice{1%tsp}, then strain.
